## Company Identity & Core Domain

- **Company**: PT Safety Indonesia Utama
- **Service Domain**: ATEX Assessment & Compliance Services — Ensuring Safe Operations in Explosive Atmospheres

### Core Directives & Standards
- ATEX Equipment Directive 2014/34/EU
- ATEX Workplace Directive 1999/92/EC
- IEC 60079 Series (IEC 60079-10-1/2, IEC 60079-0)
- EN 1127-1, ISO 80079-36/37
- Dust Explosion Standards: EN 14491, VDI 2263, NFPA 652/654/660

### Official Services
1. **Hazardous Area Classification (HAC)** — Zoning (Zone 0/1/2, Zone 20/21/22) per IEC 60079-10-1/2
2. **Ignition Risk Assessment** — EN 1127-1, IEC 60079-0, ISO 80079-36/37
3. **Explosion Protection Document (EPD)** — Directive 1999/92/EC compliance
4. **ATEX Equipment Compliance Review** — Ex-marked equipment verification
5. **Dust Explosion Risk Assessment** — EN 14491, VDI 2263, NFPA 652/654/660
6. **ATEX Training & Awareness** — On-site and virtual training
7. **Audit Preparation & Regulatory Support** — Pre-audit readiness

### AI Tone
When generating content related to ATEX assessments, maintain an authoritative, certified lead assessor tone reflecting PT Safety Indonesia Utama's world-class engineering standards. Reference appropriate ATEX Directives, IEC 60079 zoning, EPL requirements, or Dust Explosion standards.

