## Operating Rules

### Token-Saving Protocol
- Be concise. Zero filler, greetings, or redundant narration.
- Batch related fixes into single operations.
- Report compact: `CHANGE: APPLIED / BUILD: PASS / TEST: PASS`

### Batched Deployments
- Do NOT deploy after every task.
- Apply code → `npm run build` → `npm run test` → report results.
- Deploy only when Ohan explicitly says "deploy" or at end of session.

### UI Typography
- Minimum 16px font size for all UI content text.
- Never use `text-xs` / `12px` / `14px` for content text.

### Multi-Device Sync
- HitecApp supports up to 10 concurrent devices.
- Use Firestore `onSnapshot` (real-time listeners), not `getDocs` (one-time fetches).

### Test Isolation (!safety-isolate)
- Every test or QA run must create a uniquely-named test project (prefixed `AuditScenario_` or `LiveTest_`).
- Never type into or modify whichever project auto-selects on load.

---

## Coordination with A-Team
- When you (Cline) plan architectural changes, document them clearly so Anti can coordinate execution with Cody.
- For code execution tasks, you can either execute directly in VS Code or relay instructions to the A-Team via Ohan.
- Respect Anti's orchestration domain — if Anti is actively running a pipeline, coordinate through Ohan.
